diff --git a/diagram-ports/provenance/plantuml-parser-admission.md b/diagram-ports/provenance/plantuml-parser-admission.md
index dc59c00..9f1a9ee 100644
--- a/diagram-ports/provenance/plantuml-parser-admission.md
+++ b/diagram-ports/provenance/plantuml-parser-admission.md
@@ -94,10 +94,28 @@ FrameKind gained one typed Literal(String) display variant for noncanonical raw
 
 The first primitive uses the already-admitted Name representation. A command's decoded spelling is at most eleven bytes and drops with its row; other first names move into tokens without an extra retained copy. Its scan/copy and any literal frame-prefix copy charge/check before retention, and all copied lexical bytes, including discarded command spellings, remain under the existing cumulative source*2 syntax quota. No input-sized container or origin index was added. FrameKind's new String variant is covered by the existing Token component of the concrete generated-symbol upper bound; all sizes are computed with size_of, not assumed from prior small enums.
 
 The grammar, generated Rust, token/nonterminal alphabet and parser tables are byte-identical to the Task 4 proof above. The exact table witness was rerun after these changes: 72 states, 25 terminals, 5849/5939 stacks at depth64/65, at most 136/138 live states, four reductions and twelve expected terminals. Thus state/symbol slot counts, epsilon/recovery behavior, diagnostic growth/simulation bounds and delivery/action cancellation intervals remain unchanged. Admission sums the newly owned frame-literal capacities before generated entry; model-vector/string growth remains checked separately. Original and fix-round primitive/alias/lifecycle/frame/note/operator/origin, tiny-limit and cancellation contracts cover these paths.
 
 ### Task 4 fix round 2: frame-header lexical eligibility
 
 Before retaining raw frame-prefix/caption text, frame and else rows validate the remaining pre-colon quoted primitives. The scan stops at the first unquoted colon that is not part of `::`, preserving literal post-colon captions. Attached, separated and quoted command spellings retain the same raw display and exact else eligibility. Unterminated quotes and unsupported quoted escapes fail through the existing Row span/origin mapping; quote byte bounds match the native primitive lexer's raw 16KiB bound. This is lexical eligibility only: generated productions still own frame structure, nesting, else and EOF.
 
 The new scan borrows the existing Row and uses only fixed-size cursors and one escape flag. It allocates no strings, tokens, containers or origin records and runs before `frame_kind` copies a raw display value. Each visited UTF-8 character charges/checks cancellation before processing, including quote/escape/colon delimiter characters; at most one extra linear scan of the pre-colon suffix is charged to the existing work budget. Retained syntax/model admission, actual capacities, generated symbol payloads and all 72-state/25-terminal stack/reduction/diagnostic bounds above are unchanged. No grammar or generated output changed.
+
+## Activity admission (Task 8)
+
+Grammar SHA256 `ca3f7156779b2fe62ac5254cffbf33901cad71b481ae3cc341f539965865570d` generates output SHA256 `965aeffbee0584b443512415e6651a25639777d2ffc6effcaee42702b2851d49` with LALRPOP 0.23.2. Actual tables contain 92 states, 27 terminals and no recovery. `/tmp/ive-task8-stack-proof.py` reads ACTION/EOF/simulated reductions and the inspected goto function. At live-opener depths 0/1/2/3/4, exhaustive delivery and diagnostic simulation reaches 11/76/684/5581/44790 stacks, all 92 states by depth3, at most 6/13/22/31/40 live states, four consecutive reductions and twelve expected terminals. Diagnostic growth peaks are 9/24/51/78/105 state bytes.
+
+The finite viable-prefix graph has 187 transitions. Independently saturating every generated shift with every simulated-reduction predecessor path yields the same 187 transitions, covering goto contexts without a sampled-depth assumption. Zero-opener transitions are acyclic. Weight-one edges shift an if/while/repeat/fork/group opener or parenthesis. Maximum prefix lengths are 9d+6 (6 at d=0). The witness checks a max-plus induction: all 92 end-state distance components are reachable at depth3; max D3=33 and D4<=D3+9 componentwise. Monotonicity/homogeneity extends the bound to every greater depth. Concrete bounds at depths8/64/65/128 are 78/582/591/1158. Output is `/tmp/ive-task8-stack-proof.json`.
+
+Lexing checks a block opener's depth/model item before buffering its token or condition/name payload. Parenthesis depth is checked before its token. The recorded combined maximum includes block and parenthesis prefixes; a closing repeat may omit its one still-live block opener, so admission reserves 9*maximum+24 (eighteen slots above the graph bound). Lists of instructions, branches and lanes fold left into the existing Block/Instruction/Branch/Condition values. Balanced conditions, guard positions, continuation placement, block pairing and EOF belong to generated productions. No row-command string reaches a semantic parser or legacy recursive route.
+
+Before generated entry, C is the next power of two above that live bound, at least eight. Admission reserves C+C/2 slots for each state/symbol vector including old/new growth; three times live+1 diagnostic state bytes; 32 diagnostic String slots including growth; and 27*32 terminal-name bytes. The actual generated state type is i8. Symbol storage is bounded by the sum of actual Token, Instruction and Branch sizes plus eight machine words, covering the inspected tuple/string/vector/Condition/Join/GroupKind variants and location/tag/padding. Actual token capacity, tracked literal capacities, BodySource adapter allowance, Builder/Lexer and Ownership sizes are included. The complete bound is checked against source_bytes*256 before the generated parser allocates. Work admission charges five units per token, four EOF reductions, all stack/diagnostic slots and 27*(live+4) diagnostic work.
+
+Each lexical token growth admits aggregate old/new token storage with retained literals/actions/adapters before the checked reserve. Literal copies are bounded to 16KiB and charged before allocation. Raw actions use fallible geometric growth, with aggregate storage admitted and prior-copy work charged before reserve; aggregate literal storage moves with the resulting token. Typed model vectors and generated string concatenations similarly admit each old/new allocation and copy before reserving, then check actual capacities. Model instructions plus extra elseif/fork lanes retain their previous item counting. Shared Ownership supplies comment/raw/quote state and Row breakpoints; literal action openings preserve trailing spaces while comment-normalized nonliteral openings trim before entering raw continuation ownership.
+
+The checked iterator cancels every delivery and attempted EOF. Retaining reductions and the final Activity reduction use the same Budget. Direct tests interrupt seven delivery/construction checkpoints, reject malformed generated streams, admit depth64/reject65 before opener retention, and reject fifth-token/model-vector growth before mutation. The unchanged 60,000-row/500ms label failure and 4,000-row linear-work/cancellation controls now use a cfg(test) document-only facade setup equivalent to their earlier prepare call; no preprocessing pass was added to those controls. Public constants/control tests separately exercise the full preprocess/document/preamble/generated facade, raw action bytes and expanded opening/continuation terminators.
+
+Generated failures map once through the immutable origin Document before the remaining layout/unmigrated-family bridge. Authored comment-gap and frozen guard-use controls verify exact spans. Runtime activity::Parser, recursive block/instruction methods, condition/parenthesized/guard/repeat-condition reparsers are removed. activity.rs retains the unchanged model and a test-only setup helper; activitytile production code is unchanged. Shared BodySource::reborrow and actual fixed-view admission match the coordinated state/tree pattern. Defaults, public APIs, dependency/lock/vendor files, fixture sources and layout assertions remain unchanged.
+
+Failure-path admission also includes the actual unfinished raw-action String capacity that remains live while generated EOF rejection runs. A separate RED observed admission accepting 15,648 bytes while overlooking a 16KiB unfinished buffer under a 25,600-byte retention allowance; the corrected complete total rejects before parser entry. Completed actions already transfer that same capacity into the literal ledger.
